2.2 Icon design style
The outline of the icon determines people’s perception, using the outline to define the boundaries of the object, perceive the shape, and the shape of the icon is determined by the design style, so the design style of the icon is an important element for users to perceive and obtain information, and can make a quick judgment. Icons can be categorized in various ways, according to the style can be divided into pictogram icons, text icons and abstract icons, according to the artistic approach can be divided into anthropomorphic icons and flattened icons, according to the use of the device environment can be divided into PC icons, mobile icons, smart wearable device icons and so on. In the static environment, researchers usually tend to start from the perspective of visual complexity [9], and study the effects of the number of icons, strokes, lines, line widths and other factors on cognitive performance. According to Feature Integration Theory [10], simple icons are easier to understand than complex icons, and complex icons take longer to understand, but in special environments, complex icons may be more accurate and efficient in conveying visual information. Hsuan Lin [11] once compared the effects of face icons and linear icons on visual attention in static environments, and found that flat icons are more attractive. In this paper, we started from the classification of linear icons, flat icons, and line-flat combination icons, and takes into consideration of HUD application environments, combines the direction of vibration and the frequency of vibration, and explores the interaction effect between different design styles, vibration directions, and vibration frequencies, so as to provide design style suggestions for the design of automotive HUDs and aviation HUD icons.
3 Experiment design
3.1 Equipment and environment
‘Razer Blade 13’ laptop, with a resolution of 1920*1080, 13.3 inches, a brightness of 423 cd/m2, and a control room brightness of 500 lx, the experimental environment was well insulated with uniform illumination and no environmental interference. Eprime 3.0 was used to present the cued stimuli, Adobe After Effect was used to edit the pseudo-randomized target stimulus video and icon vibration effects, and Hololens was used to play the video of the experimental material.
3.2 Experiment Subjects
Twenty subjects participated in this experiment (11 males and 9 females), all of whom were master’s degree students at Southeast University, with the age range of the subjects ranging from 23-26, and all of whom did not have color blindness or color deficiency and had normal corrected visual acuity (over 1.0).
3.3 Experiment material Design
In this paper, the object of research is the vibration of the driving environment in the pixel information, select the icon as the experimental material is more illustrative, so the commonly used icons in the automotive interactive interface were selected, the design styles were linear, filled, combined linear and filled icons, each group of icons in the shape of a high degree of proximity to the semantic meaning of icons in different design styles is the same, not due to the change in design styles lead to semantic ambiguity, the experimental paradigm in this study was improved based on the visual search paradigm . In the context of Hololens, black and transparency are perceived subjectively as indistinguishable, necessitating a design approach that prevents icons from merging into the background environment. Consequently, the experimental stimulus icon design eschews the use of black hues and instead selects icon colors that exhibit a pronounced contrast with the surrounding environment, ensuring that the icons remain distinct and easily discernible. Currently for the HUD depth of field design is fixed, for the HUD depth of field design of the numerical value is not a unified standard, according to research of Li, K. [12], previous scholars have suggested that the symbol text is placed at a distance of about 2 meters from the user’s eyes, there is also a proposal to be placed at 4-8 meters, the aviation field placed in the depth of field of the HUD design is usually located in the infinite distance. The ground transportation community generally agrees that the focus of the display should be between 2.0-2.5 meters. The current mainstream HUD focal design was adopted in this experiment, with the distance of the icon imaging surface set to approximately 2.5m from the subject.
3.4 Experiment variables
The design styles of the icons in the experiment were divided into three kinds, each design style totaled 49, presenting a 7 × 7 combination arrangement, according to the human eye on the visual sensitivity range study, the effect of vibration on the human eye perception and visual performance is mainly manifested in the lowfrequency interval from 2 to 20 Hz, with a sensitivity amplitude of 1.66 mm, in this paper, we set the amplitude frequency of the amplitude of the three levels of 5Hz, 10Hz and 20Hz, the amplitude is set at 1.66 , the vibration direction is horizontal, vertical and random. Therefore, this experiment was designed with a total of: 3 icon styles × 3 vibration frequencies × 3 directions=27 experimental combinations, with each case occurring randomly 4 times, for a total of 108 trials.
3.5 Experimental process
Ensure that the subjects are well rested to maintain a good mental state before the experiment, followed by an explanation and a practice experiment, subjects will be informed of the experimental procedures and operational requirements, the distance between the subject’s eyes and the screen is about 70cm, the screen in Hololens is adjusted to a distance of 2.5m away from the subject’s eye position, after each set of experiments the subjects will be given a 10-minute break to allow the eyes to remain relaxed, to avoid visual transient effect.
